= Question 14

Given that $sin alpha = frac(5, 13)$, where $alpha$ is in Quadrant II, and $cos beta = frac(2, 5)$, where $beta$ is in Quadrant IV, find the exact value of: a) $cos (alpha + beta)$ b) $sin 2 alpha$



== Solution

a)

#image("assets/cc9001ad-6312-43bc-93f7-8b12c5460552-17_445_443_741_215.jpg", width: 20.8%)

$x ^(2)+ y ^(2)  = r ^(2) \ x ^(2)+ 25  = 169 \ x ^(2)  = 144 \ x  = ± 12 \ x  = - 12$

$cos (alpha + beta)  = cos alpha cos beta - sin alpha sin beta \  = (- frac(12, 13))(frac(2, 5))- (frac(5, 13))(- frac(sqrt(21), 5)) \  = - frac(24, 65)+ frac(5 sqrt(21), 65) \  = frac(5 sqrt(21)- 24, 65)$

b)

$sin 2 alpha  = 2 sin alpha cos alpha \  = 2 (frac(5, 13))(- frac(12, 13)) \  = - frac(120, 169)$

$x ^(2)+ y ^(2)  = r ^(2) \ 4 + y ^(2)  = 25 \ y ^(2)  = 21 \ y  = ± sqrt(21) \ y  = - sqrt(21)$

#image("assets/cc9001ad-6312-43bc-93f7-8b12c5460552-17_447_466_709_1444.jpg", width: 21.9%)

